>
  <p>
    bla5k respects the intellectual property rights of others and expects the same of our
    visitors and partners. This page explains our copyright policy and how to report content
    you believe infringes your copyright, in line with the
    <strong>Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA)</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Our copyright policy</h2>
  <p>
    bla5k is a directory of links and information about third-party tools, websites, and
    services. We do not host user-uploaded media, and we do not host or store copyrighted
    files — including movies, music, software, or ebooks. Our listings link to
    <strong>official, licensed sources only</strong>, and we do not add sites that distribute
    pirated or copyright-infringing content.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a listing includes a description, screenshot, logo, or excerpt, it is provided for
    informational purposes only, typically under fair use (criticism, commentary, and
    identification of the listed product or service). If you believe any content on this
    Site infringes your copyright, you may file a notice as described below, and we will act
    promptly.
  </p>

  <h2>Filing a DMCA takedown notice</h2>
  <p>
    To report content you believe infringes your copyright, please send a written notice that
    includes all of the following information:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your identification</strong> — your full legal name, mailing address, telephone number, and email address.</li>
    <li><strong>Identification of the copyrighted work</strong> — the work you claim is infringed, or a representative list if multiple works are involved.</li>
    <li><strong>Identification of the infringing material</strong> — the specific URL(s) or location(s) on bla5k where the material appears, with enough detail for us to locate it.</li>
    <li><strong>Your statement of good faith</strong> — a statement that you have a good-faith belief the use is not authorized by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law.</li>
    <li><strong>Your statement of accuracy</strong> — a statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information in your notice is accurate and that you are the copyright owner or authorized to act on the owner's behalf.</li>
    <li><strong>Your signature</strong> — a physical or electronic signature of the copyright owner or authorized representative.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where to send your notice</h2>  <p>
    Send DMCA notices to our designated agent:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:dmca@bla5k.com">dmca@bla5k.com</a></li>
    <li><strong>Subject line:</strong> DMCA Takedown Notice</li>
    <li><strong>Alternative:</strong> use our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> and mark the message “DMCA Takedown Notice”.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We respond to valid notices promptly, usually within 1–3 business days. Under the DMCA,
    knowingly submitting a false or misleading notice may subject you to liability. Please
    make sure your claim is legitimate before filing.
  </p>

  <h2>Counter-notification</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe material was removed or disabled by mistake or misidentification, you may
    send a counter-notification. It must include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, address, phone number, and physical or electronic signature.</li>
    <li>Identification of the material removed and its prior location.</li>
    <li>A statement, under penalty of perjury, that you have a good-faith belief the material was removed by mistake or misidentification.</li>
    <li>Your consent to the jurisdiction of the federal district court for your judicial district (or, if outside the U.S., any judicial district in which bla5k may be found), and your agreement to accept service of process from the party who filed the original notice.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Repeat infringers</h2>
  <p>
    In appropriate circumstances, bla5k will terminate the accounts or listings of repeat
    infringers, consistent with the DMCA and our own quality standards.
  </p>

  <p><em>This policy is provided for informational purposes and is not legal advice. Consult a qualified attorney if you have specific legal questions.</em></p>
</Page>
